title: Text that hangs and wraps
intro: A Text's lines can hang from its entity or stand on it, and break between words to fit a width.
project: Empty | Text Wrap

chapter: Wrapping to a width | Text > Wrap Width
create: Text
rename: Contract
set: Transform.Position = -4, 3, 0
set: Text.Size = 0.5
set: Text.Value = Deliver forty crates of copper wire to the north dock before the end of the third shift. Pay on delivery.
look: 0, 1, 5
say: A long sentence on a Text runs off in one line.
set: Text.WrapWidth = 7
expectvalue: Contract.Text.WrapWidth = 7
explain: field:Text.WrapWidth | Wrap Width | Wrap Width breaks its lines between words so none is wider than seven units, measured with the font's own letters.

chapter: Hanging from the top | Text > Vertical Align
set: Text.Align = Left
set: Text.VerticalAlign = Top
expectvalue: Contract.Text.VerticalAlign = Top
explain: field:Text.VerticalAlign | Vertical Align | With Vertical Align set to Top, the first line's top sits at the entity, and the rest hang below it.
set: Text.Value = Deliver forty crates of copper wire to the north dock before the end of the third shift. Pay on delivery. Bonus for every crate over forty, and a fine for every crate short.
explain: scene | Scene view | More text adds lines underneath: the first line stays put, so a contract or a log never needs placing by hand as it grows.
say: Bottom does the opposite, standing the last line on the entity, for a chat whose new lines push the old ones up. Middle, the default, centers them as before.

chapter: Typed out in place | Typewriter
add: Typewriter
play
wait: 3
say: A typewriter types the wrapped text where it will end up, so a word never starts at the end of a line and jumps to the next.
stop
